<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia cuts October palm olein export tax.</title>
<headline>Indonesia cuts October palm olein export tax.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's export tax on RBD palm olein will be lowered to $30 per tonne in October from $47.60 in September, the finance ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tax on crude palm oil will, however, be raised to $35.28 from $34.16 last month, the ministry said in a statement faxed to Reuters.  </p>
<p>The ministry said the export tax on RBD palm oil would be $25.76 per tonne against $33.04 in September while that on crude olein would be $33.75 per tonne, compared with $51.10.</p>
<p>The export taxes, introduced in September 1994, are based on a composite average of international prices in the last two weeks of the previous month.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom + 6221 384-6364</p>
